INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "ai_messages" ("id", "conversation_id", "role", "content", "citations_json", "confidence", "safety_flag", "created_at") VALUES ('msg_msugs3z5pd8omdh0','conv_msugs3y0tuf1pr60','assistant','Based on the GHBC regulatory source library, the following sources are most relevant to "Do I need a sprinkler for my building?".

1. GS 1207:2018, Part 4 §4.15, 4.15.11.11.2 (mechanical): EXCEPTIONS: Ducts need not be provided with automatic sprinkler protection as follows:

2. GS 1207:2018, Part 32 §32.4, 32.4.5.2 (planning): EXCEPTIONS: Open parking garages need not be equipped with an automatic sprinkler system.

3. GS 1207:2018, Part 11 §11.3, 11.4.7 (fire): Outdoor areas used exclusively for service of the building need only have one means of escape.

4. GS 1207:2018, Part 28 §28.13, 28.13.1.8 (dimensional): Sample calculation of need for protection A hospital building is 10m high and covers an area of 70m x 12m.

5. GS 1207:2018, Part 13 §13.7, 13.7.3 (electrical): Electrical generators used only for emergencies are exempt from the limits on sound levels within the building and need only meet daytime limits for sound-reaching boundaries.

6. GS 1207:2018, Part 4 §4.2, 4.2.5 (mandatory): Sprinkler protection for the tenant spaces of an open mall building shall be independent from that provided for anchor buildings.

