5. GS 1207:2018, Part 11 §11.11, 11.11.5.2 (mandatory): The riser height shall be measured vertically between the nosings of adjacent treads.

6. GS 1207:2018, Part 11 §11.11, 11.11.14.1 (mandatory): The riser height shall be measured vertically between the leading edges of adjacent treads.

GHBC interpretation — not an official determination by the issuing authority. Professional verification required. The LLM copilot is unavailable; this is a deterministic retrieval answer.','[{"requirement_id":"GHBC-REQ-009815","source_document":"GS 1207:2018","part":11,"section":"11.11","clause":"11.11.5.2","page":533,"snippet":"Stair riser heights shall be 178 mm (7 inches) maximum and 102 mm (4 inches) minimum.","status":"verified"},{"requirement_id":"GHBC-REQ-009928","source_document":"GS 1207:2018","part":11,"section":"11.11","clause":"11.11.15.2","page":537,"snippet":"The maximum riser height shall be 241 mm (91/2 inches).","status":"verified"},{"requirement_id":"GHBC-REQ-004558","source_document":"GS 1207:2018","part":6,"section":"6.6","clause":"6.6.18.1.3","page":291,"snippet":"The maximum height of riser shall be 190mm for residential buildings and 150mm for other buildings and these shall be limited to 15 per flight.","status":"verified"},{"requirement_id":"GHBC-REQ-009845","source_document":"GS 1207:2018","part":11,"section":"11.11","clause":"11.11.5.4.1","page":534,"snippet":"Where the bottom or top riser adjoins a sloping public way, walkway or driveway having an established grade and serving as a landing, the bottom or top riser is permitted to be reduced along the slope to less than 102 mm (4 inches) in heigh","status":"verified"},{"requirement_id":"GHBC-REQ-009816","source_document":"GS 1207:2018","part":11,"section":"11.11","clause":"11.11.5.2","page":533,"snippet":"The riser height shall be measured vertically between the nosings of adjacent treads.","status":"verified"},{"requirement_id":"GHBC-REQ-009918","source_document":"GS 1207:2018","part":11,"section":"11.11","clause":"11.11.14.1","page":536,"snippet":"The riser height shall be measured vertically between the leading edges of adjacent treads.","status":"verified"},{"requirement_id":"GHBC-REQ-024156","source_document":"GS 1207:2018","part":30,"section":null,"clause":"30.4.1.4.3","page":1277,"snippet":"supply in storage tanks, capacity of fuel pumps, arrangements of wet riser-cumdowncomer and wet riser installations for buildings above 15 m in height, depends upon the occupancy use.","status":"needs_verification"},{"requirement_id":"GHBC-REQ-010115","source_document":"GS 1207:2018","part":11,"section":"11.15","clause":"11.15.4","page":544,"snippet":"The triangular openings at the open sides of a stair, formed by the riser, tread and bottom rail shall not allow passage of a sphere 152 mm (6 inches) in diameter.","status":"needs_verification"}]',0.6774901375225523,'REVIEW_REQUIRED','2026-08-15T15:48:42.638Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "ai_messages" ("id", "conversation_id", "role", "content", "citations_json", "confidence", "safety_flag", "created_at") VALUES ('msg_msujwcv7xxfvax9t','conv_msujwcv7ej18bs9j','user','What is the maximum stair riser height?','[]',NULL,NULL,'2026-08-15T15:48:43.171Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "ai_messages" ("id", "conversation_id", "role", "content", "citations_json", "confidence", "safety_flag", "created_at") VALUES ('msg_msujwd5za23uv6dq','conv_msujwcv7ej18bs9j','assistant','Based on the GHBC regulatory source library, the following sources are most relevant to "What is the maximum stair riser height?".

1. GS 1207:2018, Part 11 §11.11, 11.11.5.2 (mandatory): Stair riser heights shall be 178 mm (7 inches) maximum and 102 mm (4 inches) minimum.

2. GS 1207:2018, Part 11 §11.11, 11.11.15.2 (mandatory): The maximum riser height shall be 241 mm (91/2 inches).

3. GS 1207:2018, Part 6 §6.6, 6.6.18.1.3 (mandatory): The maximum height of riser shall be 190mm for residential buildings and 150mm for other buildings and these shall be limited to 15 per flight.

4. GS 1207:2018, Part 11 §11.11, 11.11.5.4.1 (conditional): Where the bottom or top riser adjoins a sloping public way, walkway or driveway having an established grade and serving as a landing, the bottom or top riser is permitted to be reduced along the slope to less than 102 mm (4 inches) in height, with the variation in height of the bottom or top riser not to exceed one unit vertical in 12 units horizontal (8-percent slope) of stair width.

5. GS 1207:2018, Part 11 §11.11, 11.11.5.2 (mandatory): The riser height shall be measured vertically between the nosings of adjacent treads.

6. GS 1207:2018, Part 11 §11.11, 11.11.14.1 (mandatory): The riser height shall be measured vertically between the leading edges of adjacent treads.

GHBC interpretation — not an official determination by the issuing authority. Professional verification required. The LLM copilot is unavailable; this is a deterministic retrieval answer.','[{"requirement_id":"GHBC-REQ-009815","source_document":"GS 1207:2018","part":11,"section":"11.11","clause":"11.11.5.2","page":533,"snippet":"Stair riser heights shall be 178 mm (7 inches) maximum and 102 mm (4 inches) minimum.","status":"verified"},{"requirement_id":"GHBC-REQ-009928","source_document":"GS 1207:2018","part":11,"section":"11.11","clause":"11.11.15.2","page":537,"snippet":"The maximum riser height shall be 241 mm (91/2 inches).","status":"verified"},{"requirement_id":"GHBC-REQ-004558","source_document":"GS 1207:2018","part":6,"section":"6.6","clause":"6.6.18.1.3","page":291,"snippet":"The maximum height of riser shall be 190mm for residential buildings and 150mm for other buildings and these shall be limited to 15 per flight.","status":"verified"},{"requirement_id":"GHBC-REQ-009845","source_document":"GS 1207:2018","part":11,"section":"11.11","clause":"11.11.5.4.1","page":534,"snippet":"Where the bottom or top riser adjoins a sloping public way, walkway or driveway having an established grade and serving as a landing, the bottom or top riser is permitted to be reduced along the slope to less than 102 mm (4 inches) in heigh","status":"verified"},{"requirement_id":"GHBC-REQ-009816","source_document":"GS 1207:2018","part":11,"section":"11.11","clause":"11.11.5.2","page":533,"snippet":"The riser height shall be measured vertically between the nosings of adjacent treads.","status":"verified"},{"requirement_id":"GHBC-REQ-009918","source_document":"GS 1207:2018","part":11,"section":"11.11","clause":"11.11.14.1","page":536,"snippet":"The riser height shall be measured vertically between the leading edges of adjacent treads.","status":"verified"},{"requirement_id":"GHBC-REQ-024156","source_document":"GS 1207:2018","part":30,"section":null,"clause":"30.4.1.4.3","page":1277,"snippet":"supply in storage tanks, capacity of fuel pumps, arrangements of wet riser-cumdowncomer and wet riser installations for buildings above 15 m in height, depends upon the occupancy use.","status":"needs_verification"},{"requirement_id":"GHBC-REQ-010115","source_document":"GS 1207:2018","part":11,"section":"11.15","clause":"11.15.4","page":544,"snippet":"The triangular openings at the open sides of a stair, formed by the riser, tread and bottom rail shall not allow passage of a sphere 152 mm (6 inches) in diameter.","status":"needs_verification"}]',0.6774901375225523,'REVIEW_REQUIRED','2026-08-15T15:48:43.559Z');
